                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f410eecf-882d-35bd-93d8-f5ba57b115b5",
                        "entry_id": "ba00e376-f10b-3c26-bbf0-2c28b091859b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "относящийся к слюде, содержащий слюду, сделанный из слюды"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "66b960ba-d2dd-4489-98e5-f0640099e499",
                                "sense_id": "f410eecf-882d-35bd-93d8-f5ba57b115b5",
                                "text": "Одноэтажный деревянный дом со слюдяными оконцами и железною крышей тянулся сажен на десять и на улицу выходил пузатым раскрашенным крылечком."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "09ed9c62-0c62-3bd0-886e-929e639d10c7",
                        "entry_id": "ba00e376-f10b-3c26-bbf0-2c28b091859b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. напоминающий слюду (блеском, цветом и т. п.), такой, как у слюды"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0874fea-f4e8-4d24-91ca-baa1da190191",
                                "sense_id": "09ed9c62-0c62-3bd0-886e-929e639d10c7",
                                "text": "Бессонные лица их были землисто-бледны, веки припухли, и глаза стали какими-то слюдяными, бесцветными, словно выеденными за ночь туманом."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c4738fa-ee93-4d39-80ae-b902f0019543",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba00e376-f10b-3c26-bbf0-2c28b091859b",
                        "target_lang_word": "mica",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mica",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1fbe7c56-abbb-3721-85b9-f7fd533eb2c4",
                                        "entry_id": "99a03a6f-ec92-364e-8aa1-3eeeb7560874",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a group of hydrous aluminosilicate minerals characterized by highly perfect cleavage, so that they readily separate into very thin leaves, more or less elastic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ab12707-38ed-42c5-98cc-f886cd40b686",
                                                "sense_id": "1fbe7c56-abbb-3721-85b9-f7fd533eb2c4",
                                                "text": "His little eyes glittered like mica discs with curiosity, though he tried to keep up a bit of superciliousness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3548c66d-ab9a-45c9-96df-89498b3f21ef",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba00e376-f10b-3c26-bbf0-2c28b091859b",
                        "target_lang_word": "micaceous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "micaceous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9fb99f8d-03c2-3ba3-9a23-d0ae63efd6d4",
                                        "entry_id": "eb9f4a85-68eb-3c53-9fa2-c8e12c4c9d92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, consisting of, containing or resembling mica."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08b45386-6393-4f75-9c02-31da487a4d01",
                                                "sense_id": "9fb99f8d-03c2-3ba3-9a23-d0ae63efd6d4",
                                                "text": "Apart from the two or three bird masks, the only other zoomorphic mask was a wolf frontlet of cedar decorated in micaceous black paint with dentalium teeth, dentalium being an important form of wealth with some of the attributes of a currency."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f23394de-e4df-4741-9530-eff56a6ddeb7",
                                                "sense_id": "9fb99f8d-03c2-3ba3-9a23-d0ae63efd6d4",
                                                "text": "Formation of alteration minerals in the host rock during deformation within the shear zone is indicated by the parallel foliation within the secondary micaceous minerals and the unmineralized host schist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16915c87-e2ea-4b94-b340-d2145af51a12",
                                                "sense_id": "9fb99f8d-03c2-3ba3-9a23-d0ae63efd6d4",
                                                "text": "In AD 1500, it would appear, the Apache and Pueblo micaceous pottery traditions were separate, if not independent, developments, and thus both Felipe Ortega and Sharon Dryflower Reyna may be correct."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8531e1bd-2ade-3de3-b2aa-f50cabc33e10",
                                        "entry_id": "eb9f4a85-68eb-3c53-9fa2-c8e12c4c9d92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "sparkling; brilliant"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d000c751-b3c9-4e16-b9e6-ab17346b794b",
                                                "sense_id": "8531e1bd-2ade-3de3-b2aa-f50cabc33e10",
                                                "text": "The book review was a micaceous example of perfection."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "335ddb8d-a0c9-4c59-abfe-f86317f971a1",
